{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-806bbe9b-1994-4e31-b246-a84db0897d2c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a647deb61595b691","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9018-zpeywim0/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9018-E002.md","content":"# Administrator GPU-hour consumption reports over selectable time ranges\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers the core chargeback reporting capability: platform administrators can view per-project GPU-hour consumption reports over administrator-selectable time ranges, computed from the metering data delivered by the GPU usage metering workstream. It implements the reporting consumption (query, aggregation, presentation) against the confirmed metering data consumption contract — it does not re-implement or alter metering collection. Reports are in GPU-hours; no currency/cost-rate modelling.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Implement report computation over the metering data per the confirmed consumption contract: per-project GPU-hour totals for administrator-selectable time ranges.\n- Provide the administrator-facing report view in the Dashboard for per-project GPU-hour consumption over the selected time range.\n- Restrict report access to platform administrators via the Dashboard's existing authentication and authorization.\n- Reconcile report figures against the metering data source for verification (reporting must not drift from the source data).\n- No metering collection logic, no currency/dollar conversion, and no export/API surface (covered separately) in this epic.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- An administrator can generate a per-project GPU-hour consumption report for an arbitrary selectable time range, and the report lists GPU-hour totals per project.\n- Report figures reconcile with the underlying metering data for a verified sample period (totals match the source data for the same range and projects).\n- Reports are computed from the metering data via the confirmed consumption contract; no metering collection is implemented or duplicated in this epic's deliverable.\n- Report access is limited to platform administrators through the Dashboard's existing authentication/authorization mechanism.\n- The implementation builds against the confirmed metering data consumption contract; if the contract's schema or access interface changes, the impact on this epic's implementation is assessed and handled before completion.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): Administrators can view per-project GPU-hour consumption reports over selectable time ranges, computed from the metering data delivered by RHAISTRAT-9990.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":40202,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-87585dba9a11245f","agent_id":"abc56259f823db85b","session_id":"ca8c4d42-2d41-4182-b458-e5ffdb2fceb6","uuid":"c9cb2dba-2022-4dd3-b42a-3cda9aff2b77","timestamp":"2026-10-26T21:35:45.997Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9018"}
