{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-126c40e5-fc2c-4df7-b69b-c2417243fef6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bb6da9924e8794a4","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9018-zpeywim0/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9018-E003.md","content":"# Report export as CSV and stable API for finance tooling\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic extends the per-project GPU-hour consumption reporting with machine-readable output: reports can be exported as CSV, and report data can be retrieved via a stable, documented API suitable for finance tooling. It builds on the report computation delivered by the consumption-reporting capability and exposes the same per-project GPU-hour figures through export surfaces. The strategy does not prescribe where the API is served; API placement and surface design are implementation decisions for the owning team (see health warnings in the decomposition summary).\n\n## Scope\n\n- Implement CSV export of per-project GPU-hour consumption reports for the same selectable time ranges as the interactive reports.\n- Implement a stable, documented retrieval API exposing report data (per-project GPU-hour totals for selectable time ranges) for finance tooling consumption.\n- Document the API contract so external consumers can depend on it without breaking changes (versioned surface).\n- Ensure exported CSV and API results are consistent with the on-screen reports for the same query parameters.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A report for any selectable time range can be exported as CSV, and the CSV contains the same per-project GPU-hour figures shown in the interactive report for the same range.\n- Report data is retrievable via the stable API for the same selectable time ranges, and API results match the on-screen report and CSV export for the same query parameters.\n- The API surface is documented and versioned so that finance tooling can consume it as a stable interface.\n- Access to the export and API surfaces follows the same administrator-oriented access rules as the interactive reports.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-2 (P1): Reports can be exported as CSV and retrieved via a stable API for finance tooling.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":40808,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-87585dba9a11245f","agent_id":"abc56259f823db85b","session_id":"ca8c4d42-2d41-4182-b458-e5ffdb2fceb6","uuid":"91b90104-9492-4092-ba02-c4084f0a6ed8","timestamp":"2026-10-26T21:35:53.096Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9018"}
