{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-2f7ef25f-d47a-4986-92d9-db92a5f9faf8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-89be336273473af3","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9018-zpeywim0/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9018-E004.md","content":"# Per-project Kueue quota attribution contract for chargeback views\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic, owned by the Distributed Workloads team, produces the validated per-project Kueue quota attribution contract that the administrator chargeback view builds against: how each project's effective Kueue quota is derived from the platform's quota objects, and which quota semantics (nominal quota, borrowing, cohort sharing) apply when consumption is shown against quota. The Distributed Workloads team owns the Kueue quota model, so this validation is a separate deliverable from the Dashboard-side work that consumes it. No metering-data work is involved — quota attribution is independent of the metering schema.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Define how a project's Kueue quota is derived for chargeback display purposes (which Kueue quota objects and queue mappings apply to a project).\n- Validate the derivation against live Kueue objects in a representative cluster configuration (projects with quota, projects without quota, and quota shared through cohorts where applicable).\n- Decide and document which quota semantics are shown when consumption is compared against quota (e.g., nominal quota versus borrowable capacity), so the chargeback view displays an unambiguous figure.\n- Deliver the documented quota attribution contract for consumption by the Dashboard-side chargeback view, including any corrections needed if validation exposes attribution gaps.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A documented per-project quota attribution contract exists, stating which Kueue quota objects and mappings determine a project's quota figure and which quota semantics apply for chargeback display.\n- The attribution is validated against live Kueue objects in a representative cluster, covering projects with and without quota (and shared/cohort configurations where present), with results recorded.\n- The Distributed Workloads team confirms the attribution is consistent with the Kueue quota model as shipped in the platform.\n- Any attribution gaps found during validation are documented with corrections or caveats that the consuming view can account for.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- Supports HLR-3 (P1): The Dashboard admin view shows current-month consumption against each project's Kueue quota — this epic supplies the validated quota attribution that view builds against.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41354,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-87585dba9a11245f","agent_id":"abc56259f823db85b","session_id":"ca8c4d42-2d41-4182-b458-e5ffdb2fceb6","uuid":"275ba103-89eb-4da1-9b8e-452ee99e78b1","timestamp":"2026-10-26T21:36:01.700Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9018"}
