rt and stable API usage for finance tooling.\n- All documentation content is technically reviewed against the implemented reporting, export, and quota-comparison behavior, with review sign-off recorded.\n- Documentation is accessible to its audience and references only behavior that ships in the platform (no aspirational content).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-4 (P2): Documentation covers report semantics (what counts as a GPU-hour) and export integration.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":42495,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-87585dba9a11245f","agent_id":"abc56259f823db85b","session_id":"ca8c4d42-2d41-4182-b458-e5ffdb2fceb6","uuid":"8f721e21-ebe1-4ee5-8f68-e320bb9e5ba9","timestamp":"2026-10-26T21:36:15.812Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9018"}
