{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8eeac78875a48f85","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9018-E002\n3\ttitle: Administrator GPU-hour consumption reports over selectable time ranges\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9018\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9018-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9018-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the metering data schema or access interface differs materially\n15\t    from the consumption contract, rework the reporting data-access layer against\n16\t    the final contract before completion; if metering data availability slips indefinitely,\n17\t    hold at the contract plus a stubbed data-access implementation and resume when\n18\t    data lands.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 0\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n23\t  existing_foundation: 1\n24\t  open_questions: -1\n25\t  external_dependency: -1\n26\t  human_process_gates: 0\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: Medium\n32\tai_implementability_score: 2\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\tbranch: null\n35\t---\n36\t# Administrator GPU-hour consumption reports over selectable time ranges\n37\t\n38\t## Description\n39\t\n40\tThis epic delivers the core chargeback reporting capability: platform administrators can view per-project GPU-hour consumption reports over administrator-selectable time ranges, computed from the metering data delivered by the GPU usage metering workstream. It implements the reporting consumption (query, aggregation, presentation) against the confirmed metering data consumption contract — it does not re-implement or alter metering collection. Reports are in GPU-hours; no currency/cost-rate modelling.\n41\t\n42\t## Scope\n43\t\n44\t- Implement report computation over the metering data per the confirmed consumption contract: per-project GPU-hour totals for administrator-selectable time ranges.\n45\t- Provide the administrator-facing report view in the Dashboard for per-project GPU-hour consumption over the selected time range.\n46\t- Restrict report access to platform administrators via the Dashboard's existing authentication and authorization.\n47\t- Reconcile report figures against the metering data source for verification (reporting must not drift from the source data).\n48\t- No metering collection logic, no currency/dollar conversion, and no export/API surface (covered separately) in this epic.\n49\t\n50\t## Acceptance Criteria\n51\t\n52\t- An administrator can generate a per-project GPU-hour consumption report for an arbitrary selectable time range, and the report lists GPU-hour totals per project.\n53\t- Report figures reconcile with the underlying metering data for a verified sample period (totals match the source data for the same range and projects).\n54\t- Reports are computed from the metering data via the confirmed consumption contract; no metering collection is implemented or duplicated in this epic's deliverable.\n55\t- Report access is limited to platform administrators through the Dashboard's existing authentication/authorization mechanism.\n56\t- The implementation builds against the confirmed metering data consumption contract; if the contract's schema or access interface changes, the impact on this epic's implementation is assessed and handled before completion.\n57\t\n58\t## HLR Traceability\n59\t\n60\t- HLR-1 (P0): Administrators can view per-project GPU-hour consumption reports over selectable time ranges, computed from the metering data delivered by RHAISTRAT-9990.\n61\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f0901c2f864f29c","agent_id":"a53ae90e14f3a23a4","session_id":"ca8c4d42-2d41-4182-b458-e5ffdb2fceb6","uuid":"c27eab5f-7dc7-431c-bb64-e857bc384747","timestamp":"2026-10-26