{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-86a502f66fbb09e9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9018-E003\n3\ttitle: Report export as CSV and stable API for finance tooling\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9018\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9018-E002\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 0\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: -1\n17\t  external_dependency: -1\n18\t  human_process_gates: 0\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: -1\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: Low\n24\tai_implementability_score: -1\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Report export as CSV and stable API for finance tooling\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tThis epic extends the per-project GPU-hour consumption reporting with machine-readable output: reports can be exported as CSV, and report data can be retrieved via a stable, documented API suitable for finance tooling. It builds on the report computation delivered by the consumption-reporting capability and exposes the same per-project GPU-hour figures through export surfaces. The strategy does not prescribe where the API is served; API placement and surface design are implementation decisions for the owning team (see health warnings in the decomposition summary).\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Implement CSV export of per-project GPU-hour consumption reports for the same selectable time ranges as the interactive reports.\n39\t- Implement a stable, documented retrieval API exposing report data (per-project GPU-hour totals for selectable time ranges) for finance tooling consumption.\n40\t- Document the API contract so external consumers can depend on it without breaking changes (versioned surface).\n41\t- Ensure exported CSV and API results are consistent with the on-screen reports for the same query parameters.\n42\t\n43\t## Acceptance Criteria\n44\t\n45\t- A report for any selectable time range can be exported as CSV, and the CSV contains the same per-project GPU-hour figures shown in the interactive report for the same range.\n46\t- Report data is retrievable via the stable API for the same selectable time ranges, and API results match the on-screen report and CSV export for the same query parameters.\n47\t- The API surface is documented and versioned so that finance tooling can consume it as a stable interface.\n48\t- Access to the export and API surfaces follows the same administrator-oriented access rules as the interactive reports.\n49\t\n50\t## HLR Traceability\n51\t\n52\t- HLR-2 (P1): Reports can be exported as CSV and retrieved via a stable API for finance tooling.\n53\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f0901c2f864f29c","agent_id":"a53ae90e14f3a23a4","session_id":"ca8c4d42-2d41-4182-b458-e5ffdb2fceb6","uuid":"ec72d98b-1c80-4e3b-95e3-8a9bd2bf29ec","timestamp":"2026-10-26T21:38:39.420Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-86a502f66fbb09e9","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9018 decomposition"}
