ic — GPU-hour definition and attribution, time-range behavior, quota-comparison meaning.\n45\t  2. Export and integration topic — CSV export usage and stable API consumption for finance tooling.\n46\t  3. Administrator usage topic — generating and reading per-project consumption reports and the current-month quota view.\n47\t- Technically review all content against the implemented behavior before publication.\n48\t\n49\t## Acceptance Criteria\n50\t\n51\t- Published documentation explains report semantics, including what counts as a GPU-hour and how per-project attribution is computed, matching the confirmed metering data consumption contract.\n52\t- Published documentation covers export integration: CSV export and stable API usage for finance tooling.\n53\t- All documentation content is technically reviewed against the implemented reporting, export, and quota-comparison behavior, with review sign-off recorded.\n54\t- Documentation is accessible to its audience and references only behavior that ships in the platform (no aspirational content).\n55\t\n56\t## HLR Traceability\n57\t\n58\t- HLR-4 (P2): Documentation covers report semantics (what counts as a GPU-hour) and export integration.\n59\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f0901c2f864f29c","agent_id":"a53ae90e14f3a23a4","session_id":"ca8c4d42-2d41-4182-b458-e5ffdb2fceb6","uuid":"05fff9b9-a1cc-4165-b3f5-f48c5fdf3600","timestamp":"2026-10-26T21:38:41.382Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8483f3ffc1aa7064","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9018 decomposition"}
